# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CCEX .gitignore
#
# Principle: ignore build artifacts only.
#
# Everything under test/regression/ is tracked on purpose -- those files are the
# reference outputs used to check whether an optimization changes the numbers.
# That includes the .process logs, matching the convention already used by
# test/code_verification/, which commits its `process` files as references too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- build artifacts --------------------------------------------------------
/bin/
/obj/
*.o
*.d

# NOTE: do NOT add a global `*.out` rule. This repo tracks 60+ legitimate .out
#       files (DFT outputs under example/hBN_VB_natab/bath/, QE outputs under
#       example/z.SpinTensorReader/). The only build .out is bin/main.out, which
#       /bin/ above already covers.

# --- python caches ----------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: many __pycache__/*.pyc are already tracked in this repo, so this rule
#       only stops NEW ones. To stop the tracked ones from showing up as
#       modified after every analyzer run, they must be untracked separately:
#           git rm --cached -r '**/__pycache__'
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- editor / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# --- run byproducts ---------------------------------------------------------
# Stray .process files from running the examples are noise, but the regression
# ones are reference data -- keep those.
*.process
!test/regression/**/*.process
